<main class="lg:ml-[532px] lg:pt-24">
  <div id="about" class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="block lg:hidden">ABOUT</h2>
    <p>I'm a software engineer who enjoys building clean, functional interfaces — the kind of thing that looks simple on the surface but has a surprising amount of thought behind the details. I care about writing code that's still easy to read six months later, which usually means more time spent naming things well than actually writing logic.</p>
    <p>Lately I've been exploring how far I can push a simple design system before it stops being simple, and I have a habit of turning "quick weekend projects" into small obsessions that take three weeks longer than planned.</p>
    <p>When I'm not at a keyboard, I'm probably applying that same instinct to some other hobby — figuring out the most needlessly precise way to do something that didn't need to be precise at all.</p>
  </div>
